<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diane de Poitiers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1500–1566</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diane de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> was a French noblewoman and the mistress of King Henry II, who was nearly twenty years her junior. She held great influence at court and received many gifts, including the duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinois">Valentinois</a> and the château of Chenonceau, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-de-medici">Catherine de' Medici</a> took back after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s death in 1559. She retired to her château of Anet.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diane-de-poitiers.jpg" alt="Diane de Poitiers" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Clouet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean_Clouet_009.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
